Product Management
-------------------

Develop a java application that stores product details as collection of objects the details include product id, name, price, company name, date of manufacturing, quantity in hand . When we store product details if the quantity in hand is < 100 , it should not be placed into data repository and deal this situation by raising an exception . Once product details are stored then sort and display the products based on diff criteria like based on price descending order, based on range of price descending order, based on price and date of manufactured combination descending order . Now execute queries to explore product details like :
based on date of manufacturing
based on price
based on company name and price
based on price top k products
based on least price k products



Inventory Management
---------------------
Create a Java program that allows users to manage an inventory by adding items with their respective quantities, removing items from the inventory, and checking the quantity of items in the inventory. If one transaction is done (for example, after adding 1 item to the inventory), the user must be allowed to choose another action until the user chooses to exit the program.
It must use an Inventory class to manage the items and an InventoryManagement class for the user interface (console).
The details inputted by the user after the program execution is not required to be persistent.